WEBVTT

00:13.120 --> 00:15.790
You are quite a mischievous man.

00:16.300 --> 00:19.170
I came very close to dying,
I'll have you know.

00:19.170 --> 00:21.000
Don't be absurd.

00:21.000 --> 00:24.750
You fled before you could
even get involved, didn't you?

00:24.750 --> 00:27.010
There was nothing I could do.

00:27.010 --> 00:29.380
I'm sure you've gotten the report.

00:29.970 --> 00:34.100
That demon was a monster
far beyond my imagination.

00:34.720 --> 00:35.770
More importantly...

00:36.290 --> 00:38.640
Not only did you fail
to dispose of Hinata,

00:38.640 --> 00:43.400
but you also made her connection
to Rimuru stronger than before.

00:43.820 --> 00:46.390
I must admit that

00:46.390 --> 00:51.280
The long-standing Falmuth has fallen,
and I imagine a new nation will be born.

00:51.680 --> 00:55.200
It is exactly what
Demon Lord Rimuru wanted,

00:55.200 --> 00:57.790
and it means your organization's scheme
is in shambles.

00:58.580 --> 01:04.130
Demon Lord Rimuru is growing Jura Forest
into the world's center of economy.

01:04.130 --> 01:06.960
We will not stand for that.

01:07.920 --> 01:10.880
Any further public activity
would be ill-advised.

01:10.880 --> 01:14.300
I believe the same is true
for your side as well.

01:16.010 --> 01:20.810
True, there is no point in trying
to assign blame for this failure.

01:21.170 --> 01:23.440
I do appreciate
that you're quick on the uptake.

01:23.440 --> 01:27.530
Let us work together to stop this
new economic threat before it begins—

01:27.530 --> 01:29.240
Wait, one moment on that.

01:30.280 --> 01:33.700
I indeed wish to maintain
a good relationship with your family,

01:34.200 --> 01:39.080
but our organization has no reason
to be hostile to Demon Lord Rimuru.

01:39.440 --> 01:40.580
How dare you...

01:42.170 --> 01:45.240
Either way, with Hinata knowing my face,

01:45.240 --> 01:48.090
it'd be difficult for me to do anything
in the Western Nations.

01:48.090 --> 01:51.840
I shall return to my homeland
and provide you with someone to replace me.

01:54.300 --> 01:56.470
We will continue our
transactions as before.

01:57.890 --> 02:00.980
As for this incident, I say we should
put it down under the bridge.

02:01.410 --> 02:02.810
Very well.

02:02.810 --> 02:05.650
I do hope you will at least refrain
from getting in our way.

02:06.090 --> 02:08.110
That goes without saying.

02:12.570 --> 02:14.110
What a detestable man.

02:14.110 --> 02:16.490
He thinks he can take advantage of me?

02:17.240 --> 02:21.500
Once this matter is done,
you guys will be next.

02:38.470 --> 02:40.470
THAT TIME I GOT REINCARNATED AS A SLIME

03:52.500 --> 03:55.670
EPISODE 59: RECONCILIATION AND AGREEMENT

03:55.670 --> 03:57.800
The Holy Emperor Louis of Lubelius.

03:58.290 --> 04:01.710
Demon Lord Valentine was
his younger brother, Roy,

04:01.710 --> 04:04.720
and he was killed by Laplace
of the Harlequins.

04:06.520 --> 04:11.440
Hinata apologized to the Crusaders
for keeping Luminus's identity a secret.

04:11.830 --> 04:14.070
We believe in you, Lady Hinata!

04:14.070 --> 04:14.790
That's right!

04:14.790 --> 04:18.250
The one we have our faith in is you,
Lady Hinata, not God Luminus!

04:19.570 --> 04:22.910
Really? Good, then.

04:22.910 --> 04:28.660
And after that, we started discussing
the future of our two nations.

04:29.160 --> 04:33.290
The Church can't acknowledge
the existence of a nation of monsters.

04:33.810 --> 04:37.550
That was the situation
when we received the request

04:37.550 --> 04:40.300
from Archbishop Reyhiem
to mobilize the Paladins.

04:40.710 --> 04:44.430
And I personally wanted
to get back at you, too.

04:44.830 --> 04:47.140
Is it about Shizu?

04:47.140 --> 04:48.180
Yes.

04:48.180 --> 04:51.450
Looking back,
I realize I was being used then, too.

04:52.020 --> 04:55.190
Being used? By who?

04:55.940 --> 04:58.190
By merchants from the Eastern Empire.

04:58.740 --> 05:02.910
Apparently, Clayman had some
merchants he was close with.

05:02.910 --> 05:05.450
Those merchants must be
from the East, then.

05:05.890 --> 05:06.870
That's right.

05:06.870 --> 05:10.960
They told me you killed Shizu.

05:11.540 --> 05:15.460
And you happened
to be staying at Engrassia.

05:16.250 --> 05:20.630
Yeah. You couldn't have
picked a worse time, either.

05:21.050 --> 05:23.500
Just remembering about it
pisses me off.

05:28.350 --> 05:31.350
Enough coercion, you upstart brat.

05:31.350 --> 05:33.650
Oh! Um, yeah, sorry.

05:36.400 --> 05:40.530
Well, it's pretty clear
those Eastern merchants are behind this.

05:40.970 --> 05:44.280
Those guys are likely the ones
who set Falmuth's King Edmaris on us, too.

05:44.620 --> 05:46.490
There's no doubt that.

05:46.490 --> 05:50.040
Reyhiem made that much clear enough
in our questioning.

05:50.440 --> 05:54.630
Demon Lord Clayman was manipulating
Falmuth from behind the scenes.

05:55.110 --> 05:58.250
And you think the Eastern merchants
mediate things for him?

05:58.250 --> 05:59.590
Yes.

05:59.590 --> 06:03.180
Clayman was trying to awaken himself
into becoming a True Demon Lord.

06:03.180 --> 06:06.550
And Falmuth was trying
to take control of this nation.

06:07.180 --> 06:09.850
The Eastern merchants
were also involved in the process.

06:10.520 --> 06:14.850
Lastly, there was "he"
who was engineering it all.

06:15.290 --> 06:17.020
"He"?

06:17.020 --> 06:19.610
The one Clayman mentioned?

06:19.610 --> 06:22.570
I used the mind-controlling stone
that he gave me!

06:22.570 --> 06:25.450
Sh-She should have been
completely under my power!

06:25.910 --> 06:28.770
For someone as small-minded as him,

06:28.770 --> 06:32.410
it is impressive that he never divulged
this person's identity until the very end.

06:32.410 --> 06:35.000
Could it be the Seven Days?

06:35.500 --> 06:41.260
What? Are you accusing the Seven Days
took action unbeknownst to me?

06:41.720 --> 06:44.050
But we cannot fully deny
that possibility.

06:44.050 --> 06:46.840
Now you're spouting
such nonsense, too, Louis?

06:46.840 --> 06:50.770
They craved your affection, Lady Luminus.

06:50.770 --> 06:52.390
What are you talking about?

06:52.790 --> 06:55.730
Affection... in other words,
your Love Energy.

06:55.730 --> 06:58.520
It has been a hundred years
since their last ceremony.

06:58.520 --> 07:00.650
Love Energy?! What's that?

07:01.040 --> 07:03.650
They all were human.

07:03.650 --> 07:07.910
Without my energy,
they're bound to grow old.

07:08.260 --> 07:12.700
They were desperate to ensure
you won't make any other "favorites."

07:13.210 --> 07:17.120
That's the reason
the Seven Days tried to kill me?

07:17.610 --> 07:18.660
I believe so.

07:18.660 --> 07:20.810
They probably intended
to help Clayman awaken,

07:20.810 --> 07:23.010
then have him fight you.

07:23.400 --> 07:27.930
And because Clayman has been defeated,
they then tried to pin me against Rimuru?

07:28.370 --> 07:30.430
Are you certain about that?

07:30.830 --> 07:35.310
It was the Clergy who introduced us
to those merchants in the first place.

07:35.710 --> 07:37.650
But hold on...

07:37.650 --> 07:39.770
Since it's Seven Days...

07:40.250 --> 07:42.110
There's one more of them left?

07:42.590 --> 07:44.320
Nothing to worry about there.

07:44.320 --> 07:47.740
I got a report earlier from
the Cardinal at Lubelius

07:47.740 --> 07:50.620
that he has eradicated Gran,
the Sunday Priest.

07:51.030 --> 07:52.740
Cardinal?

07:52.740 --> 07:56.500
Oh, that Nicolaus guy who was
infatuated with you, wasn't he?

07:56.500 --> 08:00.130
How did he do it?
To defeat that Granville.

08:00.130 --> 08:02.960
It wasn't the most heroic approach,

08:03.330 --> 08:06.760
but he took him by surprise with
a Disintegration spell he set up in advance.

08:07.220 --> 08:09.890
His age must've taken a toll on him.

08:09.890 --> 08:12.260
For him to fall for a trap like that...

08:12.600 --> 08:16.680
By "Granville," do you mean Gran,
the Sunday Priest?

08:17.060 --> 08:18.980
That's his real name.

08:18.980 --> 08:21.480
He was known as the Hero of Light.

08:21.480 --> 08:24.190
He even fought me once.

08:24.650 --> 08:25.880
But well...

08:25.880 --> 08:29.160
Anyone who calls themselves a Hero
usually finds themselves bound by fate.

08:29.160 --> 08:35.200
Perhaps he resented me,
somewhere deep in his heart.

08:35.870 --> 08:38.580
Well, that's a relief, at least.

08:39.920 --> 08:46.630
If we hadn't noticed these merchants,
I would've started to suspect Yuuki.

08:47.170 --> 08:48.420
Yuuki?

08:48.420 --> 08:50.890
As in Yuuki Kagurazaka
the Grandmaster?

08:50.890 --> 08:55.140
Yeah. He's the most suspicious guy around,
considering the situation,

08:55.140 --> 08:58.020
but he would have no reason
to make Hinata and me fight.

08:58.520 --> 09:01.110
Yuuki, a suspect... huh.

09:01.110 --> 09:03.480
I don't think we can
completely rule him out.

09:04.020 --> 09:06.980
Whoa, you're doubting someone
from your own homeland?

09:06.980 --> 09:11.030
Oh? I'm only considering
every possibility.

09:11.530 --> 09:16.290
For that matter, I think it's a bit early
to assume the mastermind is gone.

09:16.650 --> 09:18.370
Yeah, you're right.

09:18.370 --> 09:19.910
It's not good to be too optimistic.

09:19.910 --> 09:22.630
We'd better inform everyone about this.

09:22.630 --> 09:23.580
Yeah.

09:23.580 --> 09:27.510
Let's keep a close eye
on this as we go forward.

09:28.510 --> 09:31.800
Today's snacks are scones
and fried potatoes.

09:31.800 --> 09:32.840
Enjoy.

09:35.810 --> 09:39.180
All right.
So about our future relations...

09:39.810 --> 09:43.400
Before that, I want to make
one thing very clear to all of us.

09:43.400 --> 09:47.190
Should I assume you've accepted
our apology for this matter?

09:47.190 --> 09:48.610
Yeah.

09:48.610 --> 09:52.070
I don't intend to drag
that problem along any further.

09:52.070 --> 09:53.410
Absolutely not.

09:53.410 --> 09:56.120
This entire incident
was clearly our fault.

09:56.120 --> 09:58.630
I'd like to compensate
for it in some way.

09:58.630 --> 10:00.450
We can strike a deal after that is done.

10:02.450 --> 10:06.720
I also don't want to put you through
such pain and not make up for it.

10:06.720 --> 10:09.000
I want to show you
as much sincerity as possible.

10:09.590 --> 10:11.720
Compensate, huh...

10:11.720 --> 10:16.890
Then can you officially recognize our nation
and form a diplomatic relationship with us?

10:17.290 --> 10:18.330
Fair enough.

10:18.330 --> 10:20.520
I have no intention of us
being close friends,

10:20.520 --> 10:24.140
and I plan to settle the score
with that lizard eventually.

10:24.490 --> 10:28.270
Well, worst case scenario,
I can just offer Veldora as a sacrifice.

10:28.270 --> 10:30.030
Wait a moment, Rimuru!

10:30.030 --> 10:32.780
You're thinking of doing
something cruel to me, aren't you?!

10:34.280 --> 10:36.620
Just your imagination,
my good friend Veldora.

10:36.620 --> 10:42.250
Wait, wait! When you talk to me like that,
it usually means you're up to no good!

10:42.250 --> 10:44.370
Shut up!
Don't get cocky with me!

10:44.370 --> 10:45.750
It's not my fault...

10:46.210 --> 10:49.160
Let us call a truce in the meantime.

10:49.160 --> 10:52.010
I'll open international relations
with you for a hundred years.

10:52.500 --> 10:54.760
You may consider it as my apology.

10:54.760 --> 10:55.970
Oh, really?

10:55.970 --> 10:58.640
Nonintervention treaty aside,

10:58.640 --> 11:00.640
but diplomacy relation, too?

11:00.640 --> 11:03.480
A diplomatic relation?
But then...

11:03.990 --> 11:06.850
Quit pestering me about this!
I've said what I meant!

11:07.350 --> 11:09.020
What's the issue?

11:09.020 --> 11:14.040
If Sir Rimuru was truly evil,
we would've been dead by now.

11:14.780 --> 11:16.240
True.

11:16.240 --> 11:18.450
We can trust in Sir Rimuru and his people.

11:18.450 --> 11:20.780
We need to cast off our prejudices
against monsters.

11:21.190 --> 11:23.290
I agree, too.

11:23.290 --> 11:26.460
Sir Soei was such a gentleman, as well.

11:27.960 --> 11:29.990
But there remains one problem.

11:29.990 --> 11:32.870
How will we explain this
in the framework of our faith's teachings?

11:32.870 --> 11:33.960
Depending on our approach,

11:33.960 --> 11:37.340
it might greatly shake people's faith
in the Western Holy Church.

11:37.340 --> 11:38.970
Don't be silly.

11:38.970 --> 11:43.430
Failing to protect those teachings
does not count as betraying me.

11:43.930 --> 11:47.950
Besides, it was simply a bunch of rules
made by the leaders at the time.

11:48.690 --> 11:51.360
What?! That's news to me.

11:51.740 --> 11:57.240
By protecting the defenseless,
we're helping them to lead happy lives.

11:58.240 --> 12:02.950
The most important thing to me is
not the teaching, but the faith itself.

12:02.950 --> 12:06.250
That itself is a contract with me,
and is an absolute law.

12:06.750 --> 12:11.500
All of you here can cast your Holy magic
thanks to the faith you have in me, right?

12:12.460 --> 12:18.840
But practically speaking, all of us have
spent our lives following that doctrine.

12:18.840 --> 12:21.100
If we easily throw
it away now, then...

12:21.600 --> 12:23.310
But we have to do it.

12:23.310 --> 12:28.100
I'm sure the other nations had noticed that
a hundred Crusaders made their way here,

12:28.100 --> 12:31.940
And the journalists saw
a Battlesage defeated, weren't they?

12:32.600 --> 12:35.860
If it became known that Hinata
and the Crusaders were defeated,

12:35.860 --> 12:37.860
it could lead to all kinds of confusion.

12:38.230 --> 12:42.370
Then how about we just say
Hinata and I dueled to a draw?

12:42.770 --> 12:44.370
Are you fine with that?

12:44.370 --> 12:46.080
Yeah, sure.

12:46.450 --> 12:47.720
But you know,

12:47.720 --> 12:53.380
there's only been a handful of times
when a human defeated a Demon Lord.

12:53.380 --> 12:55.500
Th-That's right!

12:55.500 --> 12:57.970
You are still just a fledgling Demon Lord.

12:57.970 --> 13:00.760
What if the other forces started
looking down on you?

13:03.180 --> 13:07.730
Benimaru, can you think of any forces here
that might try to interfere with us?

13:07.730 --> 13:08.680
None, sir.

13:09.270 --> 13:11.650
If anyone was foolish enough to try,

13:11.650 --> 13:13.860
I would twist their heads off
with my bare hands.

13:14.440 --> 13:16.750
You sound pretty confident.

13:16.750 --> 13:19.450
In that case, I don't have any objection.

13:19.450 --> 13:22.820
I'll be glad to take
advantage of your proposal.

13:22.820 --> 13:25.660
Let's take this opportunity
to announce to the world

13:25.660 --> 13:27.950
that the people of this nation
aren't evil at all!

13:28.390 --> 13:31.370
True! As a matter of fact,
everyone here's so nice to us!

13:31.770 --> 13:36.340
There had been some debate over whether
demi-humans counted as monsters or not.

13:36.340 --> 13:39.970
But that's just a prejudice
narrowing the people's view...

13:40.510 --> 13:42.890
...is what I believe.

13:42.890 --> 13:46.810
Demi-humans are
a formidable foe against humans,

13:46.810 --> 13:49.980
but dwarves are certainly part of humanity.

13:50.390 --> 13:55.730
Then why don't we mix King Gazel into this
and sign a hundred-year friendship treaty?

13:55.730 --> 13:58.480
If we can get him to guarantee
that we won't attack people

13:58.480 --> 14:00.400
that ought to change a few minds, right?

14:00.900 --> 14:02.030
Yes.

14:02.030 --> 14:05.240
If we can just build a little trust,
it'd be easier to convince people.

14:05.240 --> 14:06.920
For our future interactions,

14:06.920 --> 14:09.910
let's have Arnaud and Bacchus
stay here in Tempest.

14:11.290 --> 14:14.880
Then we will build
a Luminist church over here.

14:19.480 --> 14:20.880
Oh right, Hinata.

14:24.040 --> 14:25.180
Is that...

14:28.430 --> 14:31.680
Your rapier I swallowed last time.

14:31.680 --> 14:33.970
I fixed it and improved it for you.

14:33.970 --> 14:36.920
That'd be better than using Moonlight,

14:36.920 --> 14:39.110
the Legend-class weapon
I gave you, regularly.

14:39.620 --> 14:41.330
Thank you, Rimuru.

14:44.360 --> 14:48.200
I supposed I should try inviting them
to stay as a polite remark.

14:48.200 --> 14:52.620
Hey, since it's getting late,
why not save your departure for tomorrow?

14:53.000 --> 14:55.120
What you'll be having
this evening, by the way?

14:55.120 --> 14:57.580
Um, sukiyaki.

14:57.580 --> 14:59.960
The hot spring was pretty good.

14:59.960 --> 15:01.760
I'm looking forward to the sukiyaki.

15:02.160 --> 15:04.010
Huh? So you're staying?

15:04.970 --> 15:07.000
Whaaat?

15:10.010 --> 15:13.390
Okay, so today's banquet is sukiyaki!

15:15.140 --> 15:18.230
Here's to our future friendship.
Cheers!

15:18.230 --> 15:19.570
Cheers!

15:26.410 --> 15:30.870
Man, being able to
get drunk sure is nice!

15:31.370 --> 15:33.080
At the last party...

15:35.580 --> 15:38.580
If you don't hold back on those,
they'll be bad for your body.

15:38.580 --> 15:40.030
You fool.

15:40.030 --> 15:44.300
No mere alcohol could take me down
when not even poison could.

15:45.920 --> 15:51.310
In fact, I'm focusing on weakening
my poison nullification so I can get drunk.

15:51.310 --> 15:54.520
Weakening your poison nullification?!
You can do that?!

15:54.520 --> 15:55.770
Of course I can.

15:55.770 --> 15:59.230
Th-Teach me! Please, I beg you!

16:07.140 --> 16:09.530
White rice? Are you serious?

16:09.530 --> 16:12.120
Don't you find this
almost selfish, in a way?

16:12.120 --> 16:15.910
Well, if you don't like it,
I'll be glad to take it away.

16:15.910 --> 16:18.460
I'm not talking about that!

16:19.040 --> 16:23.740
Still... Being able to so perfectly replicate
the food from the other world...

16:23.740 --> 16:25.960
It's more exasperating
than surprising, in a way.

16:26.470 --> 16:28.340
I can't believe in just two years,

16:28.340 --> 16:31.050
you've created such a comfortable
living environment.

16:31.050 --> 16:33.350
Go ahead!
Praise me to your heart's content!

16:33.350 --> 16:34.990
Don't be stupid.

16:34.990 --> 16:38.600
I heard stories about you from Yuuki,
but I took them all with a grain of salt.

16:39.100 --> 16:41.310
No, I'm far from done yet.

16:41.310 --> 16:43.000
Transport's still super-slow,

16:43.000 --> 16:45.360
and it takes forever
to transmit information.

16:45.730 --> 16:47.690
There's just way too little entertainment.

16:47.690 --> 16:52.070
I want to build the foundation for things
like manga or something.

16:52.070 --> 16:53.700
Entertainment?

16:53.700 --> 16:58.120
In this harsh world where people are
working desperate to even see another day?

16:58.540 --> 17:01.630
We'll make sure monsters and things
are no longer a threat.

17:04.340 --> 17:06.840
I'm just gonna say this
'cause there's no point hiding it,

17:06.840 --> 17:10.050
But we're trying to make Youm a king,
build a new nation,

17:10.050 --> 17:13.550
and use that to get the Western Nations
into our sphere of influence.

17:14.020 --> 17:16.060
Just what exactly are you planning?

17:16.060 --> 17:20.640
First, we plan to get human society
to recognize us.

17:20.640 --> 17:23.560
Well, this part was already halfway done.

17:23.560 --> 17:27.570
The leaders of many nations
are now aware of who we are,

17:27.570 --> 17:31.410
and the merchants and adventurers
are spreading rumors about us.

17:31.410 --> 17:33.410
After that came our road infrastructure.

17:33.410 --> 17:36.580
Safe and efficient trade routes
are being built as we speak.

17:36.580 --> 17:39.080
And lastly, information transfer.

17:39.080 --> 17:44.000
Only those who can wield magic
can use the communication crystals

17:44.000 --> 17:47.750
So we got our eyes on
Sticky Steel Thread and magisteel!

17:47.750 --> 17:49.550
When I tested it out myself,

17:49.550 --> 17:53.090
and my transmission over the thread
was pretty astounding!

17:53.090 --> 17:57.680
It makes use of magicules, so relatively
smooth communication is possible!

17:57.680 --> 18:00.270
The same goes for when using magisteel.

18:00.270 --> 18:03.270
Using these, it could
be possible to build

18:03.270 --> 18:06.400
a communication network
between nations and villages!

18:08.810 --> 18:12.900
That'll be super useful when it's done,
don't you think?

18:12.900 --> 18:18.160
Look, this kind of information is usually
kept confidential, did you know that?

18:18.160 --> 18:19.940
Oh, you're right.

18:19.940 --> 18:22.270
Maybe I got carried away
and said too much.

18:22.270 --> 18:23.790
Must have been the alcohol talking.

18:23.790 --> 18:24.750
Report.

18:24.750 --> 18:27.590
Restarting Ailment Nullification.

18:27.590 --> 18:32.300
Also, this resistance cannot
be adjusted for the time being.

18:32.300 --> 18:33.490
What?!

18:34.340 --> 18:37.140
Oh, no.
I'm getting sober...

18:37.500 --> 18:41.890
And if you go too far,
the angels are going to attack you.

18:41.890 --> 18:43.390
Hm? Angels?

18:43.390 --> 18:48.020
They'll come running to cities
that have become far too advanced.

18:48.020 --> 18:52.190
I would love to exterminate
those annoying flies,

18:52.190 --> 18:54.780
but then everyone would know my identity.

18:55.210 --> 18:59.160
Though because of that moron,
the Crusaders know about me now.

18:59.160 --> 19:00.290
It's not my fault.

19:00.790 --> 19:02.660
Angels, huh...

19:02.660 --> 19:06.040
If they come to strike us,
we'll simply fight back.

19:07.330 --> 19:09.500
I figured you would say that.

19:09.500 --> 19:12.920
We might even be fighting on
the same side, when the time comes.

19:13.340 --> 19:17.800
I have no intention of watching
my city be destroyed a second time.

19:17.800 --> 19:20.600
Not by those flies and not by that lizard!

19:20.600 --> 19:21.520
It's not my fault...

19:21.520 --> 19:25.890
Now, now, let's save
the big talk for later.

19:25.890 --> 19:30.320
Lady Hinata, and if you aren't
eating that meat, I'll take it!

19:30.320 --> 19:33.820
Fritz...
Do you have a death wish?!

19:33.820 --> 19:37.910
H-Huh?! Lady Hinata,
you're looking so... serious...

19:41.660 --> 19:46.290
Afterward, the Holy Empire of Lubelius
suddenly announced

19:46.290 --> 19:51.840
the Dwarven Kingdom as a land of humans
it could potentially become allies with.

19:51.840 --> 19:57.010
They also formally announced diplomatic
relations with the Jura Tempest Federation,

19:57.010 --> 20:02.430
and albeit one with a time limit,
as well as a nonaggression pact.

20:03.680 --> 20:07.940
Now we can continue to use them as a point of
contact for negotiation with the Five Elders.

20:08.320 --> 20:09.560
Yes.

20:09.560 --> 20:11.370
But still, those sly foxes...

20:11.370 --> 20:14.690
Pushing a monster like that on me...

20:16.110 --> 20:17.740
That must've been quite a disaster.

20:17.740 --> 20:19.200
Indeed it was.

20:19.780 --> 20:22.160
Diablo, if I recall.

20:22.160 --> 20:26.710
He's a fearsome demon, one who might even
be the equal of Blanc over in the Empire.

20:27.290 --> 20:32.090
To be honest, I think a frontal assault
against them would be a pretty bad idea.

20:32.500 --> 20:35.090
I wouldn't go so far
as to call it unwinnable.

20:35.090 --> 20:37.590
But I doubt Cerberus
would survive the battle.

20:38.000 --> 20:41.050
I used Hinata to get back at 'em a little,

20:41.050 --> 20:42.970
but that sure didn't work out.

20:42.970 --> 20:45.310
So let's lay low for a while.

20:45.710 --> 20:49.390
Still, the Five Elders
were all bark and no bite.

20:49.390 --> 20:51.190
I thought that would happen.

20:51.190 --> 20:55.570
Demon Lord Rimuru is too soft,
so I doubt he would kill Hinata.

20:55.990 --> 21:01.570
I was kind of hoping that softness
would spell his downfall, though...

21:02.040 --> 21:04.450
If you hadn't contacted me,

21:04.450 --> 21:09.210
I would've had to duel Saint Hinata herself
in front of Demon Lord Rimuru.

21:09.210 --> 21:11.460
If I had lost you,

21:11.460 --> 21:15.590
my plan would've been
sabotaged beyond repair.

21:15.590 --> 21:19.720
Well, at least I managed
to escape for you.

21:21.590 --> 21:24.100
But don't go all out, okay?

21:24.100 --> 21:27.470
I still want to sit and watch
to see how this struggle plays out.

21:27.470 --> 21:31.850
In that case, it might be best for me
to return to my homeland.

21:31.850 --> 21:33.980
I'm thinking of having
Misha fill in for me.

21:33.980 --> 21:36.480
Yeah. Let's go with that.

21:36.480 --> 21:38.440
Understood.

21:38.440 --> 21:44.740
So how should we wind down the slave trade
I had been working on here?

21:45.580 --> 21:47.540
Oh, right, there was that, too, huh?

21:47.540 --> 21:50.370
They're a pain anyway,
let's shut the Orthrus Slave Market down.

21:50.370 --> 21:53.880
Are we releasing all the rare monsters
at Misha's Echidna Club?

21:54.540 --> 21:58.510
No, anything designated confidential
should be treated the same as always.

21:58.510 --> 22:01.680
We still have a link to the Rosso family,
after all.

22:02.190 --> 22:05.430
Very well. I'll leave the rest
in your capable hands.

22:11.430 --> 22:13.940
You were listening weren't you, Kazalim?

22:14.370 --> 22:15.900
I sure was, Boss.

22:15.900 --> 22:19.190
So why are you intent
on dismantling Orthrus now?

22:19.570 --> 22:20.990
It's simple.

22:20.990 --> 22:24.610
I thought I'd let him play
the good guy on this.

22:24.610 --> 22:26.700
Him?

22:26.700 --> 22:29.040
Oh, that guy?

22:29.040 --> 22:31.960
You come up with the most
interesting ideas sometimes, Boss.

22:32.410 --> 22:33.540
I know, right?

22:33.540 --> 22:35.710
Can I have you handle
that matter, then?

22:36.170 --> 22:37.420
Of course.

22:37.420 --> 22:39.670
Also, not to change the subject,

22:39.670 --> 22:42.090
but can you call me Kagali?

22:42.800 --> 22:46.050
Oh, you're finally going through with it?

22:46.470 --> 22:47.680
Yeah.

22:47.680 --> 22:50.470
With Clayman dead,
I made up my mind.

22:51.060 --> 22:53.020
Until I have my revenge against Leon,

22:53.020 --> 22:55.770
I'm putting the name
Demon Lord Kazalim on ice.

22:55.770 --> 22:57.400
Sure thing.

22:57.400 --> 23:00.780
In that case, get to work, Kagali.

23:01.170 --> 23:03.030
Yes, Boss.

24:36.700 --> 24:39.170
Next time, "The Preparation."
